From 2f1c0406cc6387a947aabcfa9fa6cefc30e01a43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:34:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: the log of a Blu-ray join says which stream
 differs, and how

Where two play items of a playlist join seamlessly but their streams
differ, the player opens its streams again and kodi.log says why, but only
with the list or the part of the clips that differed ("audio streams",
"the elementary streams of the clips"): one log of a disc with several cuts
could not tell which stream stopped the join, nor whether the check that
stopped it was one that the streams the player uses need.

BlurayJoin.h now says, in the same place, the list, the stream (its number
and PID) and every value that differs, as the play item before has it ->
as the next one has it ("audio stream 2 of 3, PID 0x1101: language eng ->
fra"); for the clips, the program, the elementary stream, the PIDs that only
one of the two carries ("PID 0x1102 with coding 0x86 only in the clip
after"), the PCR PID with its sequence and its clip, and the counts. The
line of each join names the clip of the play item before too.

What is compared, and so the verdict, is unchanged: SameStream() and
SameClipStream() decide as before, and the text is made only where they
said no. Checked on the host against the decision of before on 400000
random pairs of play items and clips: the same verdict in every case.
